    "explanation": "Both of you: the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00703 is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nA no-show fee is only chargeable if the driver actually arrived at the pin and waited. On this record he did not, and the failure is on the face of the documents. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00703) contains no driver 'arrived' event at all — arrived_at is null — so POL-NS-01 limb (a) fails at once; and the trip was terminated by the rider (status CANCELLED_BY_RIDER, cancelled_by RIDER), not by the driver with a RIDER_NO_SHOW trigger, so limb (d) fails as well.\n\nThe driver's own telemetry agrees. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00703) holds 25 fixes at 10-second cadence from 05:30:00 to 05:34:00, and every fix places the driver between 19,176 m and 19,330 m from the pickup pin — roughly 19 km away. For this STANDARD pickup the arrival radius is 50 m and the required dwell is 300 seconds. The trace returns 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds, a 300-second shortfall. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails and POL-NS-02 entitles the rider to a full refund of the cancellation fee; POL-NS-06 reaches the same result on the dwell arithmetic alone. The driver's statement in the dispute — 'I overslept and had not reached the pickup when she cancelled' — is an admission against his own interest and confirms what the telemetry shows; it carries no weight multiplier and so does not itself move confidence.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and no limb of POL-NS-01 is satisfied; POL-NS-06 displaces POL-NS-07 and directs that no compensation is payable. The SGD 4.80 driver_compensation figure in the fare breakdown's derived block has no clause behind it on these facts. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee either: its 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling is measured from the pickup pin and is not remotely met at ~19 km. POL-NS-04 is not relied on by either side (the chat log, EV-CHAT-00703, is empty and the trace carries no rider track), and nothing on the rider's conduct changes the outcome.\n\nOn amounts: the only sum in play is the SGD 6.00 cancellation-fee line in EV-FARE-00703 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). That figure reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule — the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee (SGD 6.00) — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect, and SGD 6.00 is the amount refunded.\n\nNo escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination against 110 completed trips; the rate is under 0.08), there are no repeat-party disputes (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0), no two admissible artifacts contradict each other, and no deciding fact rests on impaired evidence. The only below-weight artifact, the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00703-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no deciding fact here — its absence merely closes the POL-NS-06(i) dwell-accumulation route, which the driver does not need. No false-arrival referral is entered: the driver never tapped 'arrived', so POL-NS-05(ii) has nothing to record."
