    "explanation": "The ruling is the same for both of you: the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable. Both advocates, and the driver's own account, ask for that outcome, and the arithmetic of the record bears it out.\n\nPOL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four of its conditions hold, and the rider breaks a fee by breaking just one. Three fail here on the face of the record. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-00703 (weight 1.0) carries no driver 'arrived' event: arrived_at, started_at and ended_at are all null. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-00703 (weight 1.0) holds 25 fixes at a 10-second cadence from 05:30:00 to 05:34:00 with 100% coverage and no gaps, and every fix puts the driver 19,176 m to 19,330 m from the pickup pin. For a STANDARD zone the arrival radius is 50 m, and the trace returns 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes, so the three consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires do not exist at any point. (c) The longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0.0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a shortfall of 300 seconds. Limb (d) also fails: the trip record shows the trip cancelled by the rider (CANCELLED_BY_RIDER, cancelled_by RIDER), not terminated by the driver.\n\nPOL-NS-02 is explicit that where the trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation the driver never arrived and the rider gets a full refund. The driver's closest fix was about 19.2 km away, so POL-NS-03's 400 m wrong-entrance route does not apply, and POL-NS-06 requires the same full refund independently: a 0-second dwell is below the 300-second minimum. The driver's statement, 'I overslept and had not reached the pickup when she cancelled,' is an admission against his own interest and agrees with the telemetry.\n\nBecause POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in any limb, POL-NS-07 cannot be reached (it compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full), so the SGD 4.80 driver_compensation figure in the fare breakdown has no clause behind it and no compensation is paid.\n\nThe SGD 6.00 figure itself is correct: it is the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee (SGD 6.00) under the fee_schedule resolution rule, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. The only artifact below weight 1.0 is the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00703-01 (weight 0.0): it carries no fact, and although its absence closes the POL-NS-06(i) dwell-accumulation route it decides nothing here. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact sits at weight 1.0, and no clock-skew, trace-gap or chat defect impairs them, so no POL-NS-09 trigger fires: the anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination, 1/110 = 0.9%), the parties share no repeat no-show disputes, and no admissible artifacts contradict each other. POL-NS-05's false-arrival machinery is not engaged because no 'arrived' event exists to be false, so no referral is entered, and no other clause produces one."
